-8e04-d71876767c8f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553892 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554496 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554335 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554496 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554496 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554496 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554496 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ac754ef8-8a92-57f1-83bb-568d71efea89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554519 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554519 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554519 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554519 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554394 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554519 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554519 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554519 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554519 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554519 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d2b10337-7261-5902-bb66-e43af38982e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186553893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554527 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186554377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554527 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554527 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554527 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186554260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554527 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e9b51d7b-17fc-5ee3-a798-42015df0b697" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554555 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554555 #edb/ref 1069 "q-22657" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554555 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554555 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6d/6d6009de9ef5df47144f36eb42393b7e9f77ab5c70e3606db09e48bf98289ecb.png)\n\nWhich of the following polygons has the same perimeter as the hexagon $ABCDEF$ shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554555 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "29ae9066-cb5e-58ca-bc97-42812b49b53a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554555 #edb/ref 1074 "The perimeter of the triangle shown below is $17$, as well as the perimeter of the given hexagon. Among the options given, the triangle is the only one that satisfies this. \n\n![](images/e4/e40d126b8304f762f95026016e13c193994fbb7f70f3173a86a35a08526a3bdb.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554609 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554609 #edb/ref 1069 "q-120787" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554609 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554609 #edb/ref 1071 "In the regular octagon $ABCDEFGH$, we have $CD=1.5\\,cm.$ What is the perimeter of the octagon?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554609 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9bda3ed0-c16c-5140-97eb-7ad72121a660" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554609 #edb/ref 1074 "The perimeter $p$ of a polygon is the sum of the measures of all its sides. Since all the sides of a regular octagon are equal and the measure of one of them is $1.5\\,cm$, we have \n\n$$\np=8\\cdot CD=8\\cdot 1.5=12\\,cm.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554635 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186554496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554635 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67871" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554635 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554635 #edb/ref 1071 "In a quadrilateral $ABCD,$ the measures of the sides are $AB=17\\,mm,$ $BC=14\\,mm,$ $CD=2\\,cm,$ and $DA=9\\,mm.$\nWhat is the perimeter of the quadrilateral?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554635 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ef8d594b-7df8-58f6-be78-cc667ee70380" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554635 #edb/ref 1074 "Most of the measures are given in $mm$ (millimeters), so we will start by converting all the measures to $mm$ and adding them up:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =17\\,mm+14\\,mm+\\overset{2\\,cm}{\\overset{⏞}{20\\,mm}}+9\\,mm \\\\  & =60\\,mm\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is a large quantity of $\\text{mm},$ we will convert to $\\text{cm}:$\n\n$$\np=60\\,mm=6\\,cm.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554648 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0c9bd898-fab7-54c1-83ae-93d8a8161ea8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554648 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186554609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554659 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554659 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2fe99cc3-cf10-59ef-aaff-06e6316d17c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554659 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186554635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554667 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186554659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554667 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3e2e88f8-0f28-5880-a50b-2393532fb354" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186554667 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186554555 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
